    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0250" n="144" xml:id="pg144"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Egan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wharton transmits to Mr. Egan information received by wire from the president
                    of the Central and South American Telegraph Company relating to the company
                    being forcibly prevented from working the cable between Iquique and Valparaiso,
                    and expressing the willingness of the company but the fear that if the direct
                    cable were connected through between Peru and Valparaiso it would be cut by the
                    officials at Iquique.</p>
            </div>
